# Common hardware firmware. live-build's --firmware-chroot default installs the
# entire non-free-firmware archive (~1.2 GiB installed); we disable that and
# install only the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth/storage blobs ordinary laptops need. The
# exotic, data-centre and SoC blobs live in the signed Firmware extension.
firmware-linux-free
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-atheros
firmware-mediatek
firmware-realtek
firmware-brcm80211
bluez-firmware
xwayland
# mesa-vulkan-drivers (79 MiB installed) moved to the Hypervisor extension.
